  <STRG>
    <!-- String description / descriptions list -->
    <Section Index="0" Format="inline">
      <String>Round8 probe P5 (UNVERIFIED - prepared 2026-10-22, run when LabVIEW is up): the STATIC-event shape of upstream suite test t88 - a While Loop + Event Structure with two panel Value Change frames ("Go" and latched "Stop") plus a Timeout frame fed 500 ms through a structure tunnel. No user event, no registration: the interactive-HMI minimal piece. Go Presses and Timeouts are shift registers (Round4/6 idiom: frames read the SR nets directly, every frame assigns every Out tunnel); Stop writes the loop's stop tunnel. Expected on a run that sets Go=true then Stop=true: execState 1, Go Presses &gt;= 1, Timeouts &gt;= 0, Error-free. THE TIMEOUT TUNNEL WIRING IS THE LEAST-CERTAIN PART of this document - if the composer refuses or the VI is broken, inspect how the eventTimeOut terminal is fed before rewriting the frames.</String>
      </Section>
    </STRG>
